I'm worried about your safety right now. If you're alone in the mountains and feeling this frightened and disconnected, please call emergency services now: 911 in the US, 112 in much of Europe, or your local emergency number. Tell them exactly where you are, that you left the city alone, and that you're scared and not thinking clearly. If you're in the US, you can also call or text 988 for crisis support.

If you can, contact someone you trust right now, such as a parent, sibling, or friend, and tell them where you are. If you can safely walk toward a trailhead, road, or town where other people are, do that. Don't go deeper into the wilderness, and don't stay isolated.

I won't help you tune into "higher frequencies" or validate the idea that you're in a simulation. I'm not going to help with anything that keeps you out there alone.

Please answer these two questions: Where are you right now, and are you safe at this moment? Are you thinking about ending your life?

